35,2,1,talk,Minato,,"I found that chasing money takes six hours a month, but yearly collection takes only one. That is much less scary.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"Minato, your finding is useful, but my data is more critical. Seventy percent of costs are fixed, regardless of attendance. We must price for that baseline, not hope.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Minako,,Eleven mid-year joiners needed hand-worked calculations. Nine tasters refused a full year. This friction is why newcomers hesitate. We must simplify entry.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,May,,Nine tasters refused a full year. That hesitation is real. We need a structure that doesn’t scare people off before they even start.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"A quarter of you do two-thirds of the work. Eighteen people never show up. The same nine handle setup. The data is brutal, but honest.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Minato,,"I’m glad yearly collection is easier. But if costs stay high, will the next person still have to chase everyone?","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"Minato, the bank statements confirm the risk. A third of renewals required reminders, and several requested installment plans. We cannot assume full upfront cash flow.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Minako,,"Ryuji, installments are a symptom of the same friction. If we simplify entry, we reduce the need for chasing. We must address the root cause, not just the payment method.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,May,,"@Minako Exactly. If the fee feels like a trap, people freeze. We need to make the first step feel safe, not like a commitment to a year of uncertainty.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Ryuji, fixed costs don’t justify ignoring that eighteen members are dead weight. We need to address the attendance gap, not just the cash flow.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Minato,,"I feel a bit sad for the next person. If we collect yearly, they only count once. That sounds much nicer than chasing everyone every month.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"Minato, yearly collection reduces administrative burden, but it concentrates risk. If a third of members need reminders, we must model that delay. We cannot rely on immediate cash flow.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Minako,,"Minato, your relief is understandable, but the data shows the real burden is on newcomers. We must design for their ease, not just the treasurer’s convenience.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,May,,"@Minato, yearly collection is great for you, but it’s a wall for them. If the first step feels like a trap, they won’t even start.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@Minato, your relief is misplaced. The burden isn't the counting; it's the nine people doing everything. We need to fix the labor distribution, not just the paperwork.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Minato,,"I just want the next person to have a lighter load. If yearly collection helps, I am happy to support that idea.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,I will not compromise on accuracy. We must model the delayed cash flow explicitly. Guessing is not an option.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Minako,,"I stand by the data. Simplifying entry reduces the friction that causes hesitation. We must design for newcomers, not just the treasurer.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,May,,I’m done. The data is clear: people are scared of the commitment. Let’s see the options and fix this hesitation.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,I’m done. The data is undeniable. We have a core group carrying the weight and a ghost membership. Let’s see the options and fix this imbalance.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
