60,3,1,talk,Minato,,"I think Option A is the kindest. It means the next person only counts once, not all year. Is that okay for everyone?","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,"Minato, Option A ignores the cash flow delays I found. A third of renewals needed reminders. We cannot assume immediate liquidity.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Minako,,"Minato, Option A’s simplicity is appealing, but it ignores the friction I found. Newcomers hesitate at the full-year commitment. We need a lower barrier to entry.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,May,,"@Minako, you’re right. A flat fee feels like a trap. Option B lets people dip a toe in without the scary full-year commitment.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,"@Minato, Option A is a joke. Eighteen ghosts pay the same as the nine doing the work. Option C lets us price actual participation, not just presence.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Minato,,"I hear you all. Option B means counting for every event, which is a lot of work. I worry the next person will be tired.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"Minato, Option B fragments revenue tracking. With fixed costs at seventy percent, per-event charges create unpredictable cash flow. We need a stable baseline to cover those obligations reliably.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Minako,,"Minato, your concern is valid, but Option B’s per-event tracking creates the very friction that scares newcomers. We need a stable baseline that doesn’t demand constant administrative attention.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,May,,"@Minato, I get the worry, but Option B is the only way to stop people freezing up. If the first step is small, they’ll actually show up.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Minato, Option B is administrative suicide. You’d be counting coins for every single event. Option C is the only way to stop subsidizing ghosts.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Minato,,"I am sorry to hear Option B is so hard. But Option C sounds confusing. I just want the next person to have a simple, quiet job.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,"Minato, Option C’s tiers create variable revenue streams, complicating the fixed-cost coverage I need to verify. We need predictable inflows to match those seventy percent fixed obligations.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Minako,,"Minato, Option C’s named levels create the exact visibility that makes newcomers hesitate. If the structure feels opaque, they won’t drift in. We need a simple, stable baseline that doesn’t demand constant administrative attention.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,May,,"@Minako, wait. Tiers feel like a judgment. If people feel judged, they freeze. Option B is the only way to keep it light and safe.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, judgment is the point. If you don’t show up, you don’t pay. Option C aligns cost with actual contribution. Stop protecting the ghosts.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Minato,,"I am sorry to hear Option B is so hard. But Option C sounds confusing. I just want the next person to have a simple, quiet job.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Ryuji,,"Minato, simplicity is not accuracy. Option A’s predictable inflow is the only way to reliably cover our fixed costs. I vote A.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Minako,,"Minato, I understand your desire for simplicity. However, Option A’s barrier is too high for newcomers. I vote B to lower that friction.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,May,,"@Minato, I hear you, but Option B is the only way to stop the hesitation. If the first step is small, people actually show up. I vote B.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Shunichi,,I vote C. The data is clear: participation should dictate cost. Stop subsidizing the ghosts.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
